message.content:
Below is a minimal example of an “interactive card” that rotates (spins) when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** – no JavaScript.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body{
    margin:0;
    padding:0;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card{
    width:250px;          /* width of the card */
    height:350px;         /* height of the card */
    perspective:800px;    /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
    cursor:pointer;       /* hand icon on hover */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card inner wrapper ---------- */
.card-inner{
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform .6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;     /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back{
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;      /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card-front{
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    color:#333;
}

.card-back{
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* place it behind the front */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    color:#555;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner{
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* flip the card */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-front">
            <h2>Front</h2>
            <p>To jest karta przednia.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-back">
            <h2>Back</h2>
            <p>To jest karta tylna.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on `.card` | Gives depth so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| 2 | `.card-inner` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements (`.card-front`, `.card-back`) in 3D space. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the back of each face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| 4 | On hover, `.card-inner` rotates 180° around Y‑axis | Flips the card to show the other side. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add images inside `.card-front` and `.card-back`.  
If you want a different rotation axis (e.g., X‑axis), change `rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` (and adjust the back face accordingly).
